<%# locals: none.

    Design editor page shell: toolbar, Explorer/Components rail, Preview/
    Structure/Code centre pane, Inspector rail. The tabler-ui--docs-editor
    Stimulus controller (docs/app/javascript/controllers/tabler_ui/docs/
    editor_controller.js) reads the values on the root element below,
    populates every data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target below from
    localStorage + GET editor/schema on connect(), and wires up every
    data-action button. Every target starts with plain server-rendered
    placeholder content (a "loading"/explanatory <p>, or -- for the
    Components tab -- the same static, non-interactive category listing
    the old placeholder used), so this page still renders sensibly with no
    JS at all; the controller simply never gets a chance to overwrite that
    content in that case. Structural add/move/delete controls are real
    buttons throughout (never drag-and-drop only) per this repo's CLAUDE.md
    -- SortableJS is a separate, purely additive enhancement another agent
    adds later.

    Deliberately does NOT call content_for(:contents) -- there is no
    per-page "Contents" rail to link to here, so the editor keeps the full
    content column the layout gives a page with none (col-lg-10, same as
    the index/forms pages -- see application.html.erb's own comment).

    Does call content_for(:wide_layout), just below -- this page's
    three-pane toolbar layout wants the whole window, not the col-lg-8/10
    the layout otherwise caps content at, so the sidebar column folds into
    a collapsed toggle and the outer container drops its max-width (see
    application.html.erb's own comment on that flag). No other docs page
    sets this.

    Both tab strips below (Explorer/Components, Preview/Structure/Code)
    reuse the tabs component's own Bootstrap-tab markup convention
    (data-bs-toggle="tabs" data-controller="tabler-ui--tab", see
    app/components/tabler_ui/tabs/_component.html.erb) rather than a bare
    tabler_ui.tabs call -- the editor's three-pane layout doesn't fit that
    component's single nav+content shape, but the Bootstrap Tab lifecycle
    underneath is the same already-registered controller, not a second
    implementation of it (rule 6). %>
<% content_for :wide_layout, true %>
<%= tabler_ui.icon icon: "layout-grid-add", class: "me-2" %>
<%= tabler_ui.page_header title: "Design editor", pretitle: "Editor" %>

<div id="tabler-ui-docs-editor"
     data-controller="tabler-ui--docs-editor"
     data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-schema-url-value="<%= editor_schema_path %>"
     data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-preview-url-value="<%= editor_preview_path %>"
     data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-csrf-token-value="<%= form_authenticity_token %>">

  <div class="docs-editor-toolbar d-flex align-items-center gap-2 mb-3">
    <span class="badge bg-secondary-lt text-secondary" data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="filename">
      index.html.erb
    </span>
    <div class="ms-auto btn-list">
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
              data-action="click->tabler-ui--docs-editor#copyErb">Copy ERB</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
              data-action="click->tabler-ui--docs-editor#download">Download</button>
      <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
              data-action="click->tabler-ui--docs-editor#exportAll">Export all</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="errors"></div>

  <div class="row docs-editor-panes">
    <div class="col-12 col-lg-3 mb-3">
      <div class="card docs-editor-rail">
        <ul data-bs-toggle="tabs" data-controller="tabler-ui--tab" role="tablist" class="nav nav-tabs">
          <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
            <a href="#docs-editor-explorer" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-tabler-ui--tab-target="toggle"
               role="tab" aria-selected="true" class="nav-link active">Explorer</a>
          </li>
          <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
            <a href="#docs-editor-components" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-tabler-ui--tab-target="toggle"
               role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="nav-link">Components</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tab-content card-body docs-editor-rail-body">
          <div class="tab-pane active show" id="docs-editor-explorer" role="tabpanel">
            <div class="btn-list mb-2">
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
                      data-action="click->tabler-ui--docs-editor#newFile">New file</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn btn-sm btn-outline-secondary"
                      data-action="click->tabler-ui--docs-editor#newFolder">New folder</button>
            </div>
            <div data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="explorer">
              <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
                The workspace's file tree renders here once a workspace is loaded.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="tab-pane" id="docs-editor-components" role="tabpanel"
               data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="palette">
            <%# Static fallback + no-JS content -- the controller replaces this
                with the schema-driven palette (docs/app/javascript/controllers/
                tabler_ui/docs/editor/palette.js), which additionally offers the
                layout kinds (row/column/heading/text/partial) this loop can't
                describe. Each item already carries the click action + data
                attributes #addFromPalette needs, so this listing keeps working
                even in the moment before the schema fetch resolves. Also
                draggable, with the same dragstart/dragend actions
                (#paletteDragStart/#paletteDragEnd) palette.js's own template
                carries -- see that file's header for why the two copies of
                this markup must stay in sync by hand. %>
            <% TablerUi::Docs::Navigation.category_names.each do |category| %>
              <h4 class="mt-2"><%= category %></h4>
              <div class="list-group list-group-flush mb-2">
                <% TablerUi::Docs::Navigation.components_in(category).each do |name| %>
                  <div class="list-group-item list-group-item-action py-1 docs-editor-palette-item"
                       data-component-name="<%= name %>"
                       draggable="true"
                       data-action="click->tabler-ui--docs-editor#addFromPalette dragstart->tabler-ui--docs-editor#paletteDragStart dragend->tabler-ui--docs-editor#paletteDragEnd"
                       data-editor-kind="component" data-editor-component="<%= name %>">
                    <%= TablerUi::Docs::Navigation.title_for(name) %>
                  </div>
                <% end %>
              </div>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-12 col-lg-6 mb-3">
      <div class="card docs-editor-rail">
        <ul data-bs-toggle="tabs" data-controller="tabler-ui--tab" role="tablist" class="nav nav-tabs">
          <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
            <a href="#docs-editor-preview" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-tabler-ui--tab-target="toggle"
               data-action="shown.bs.tab->tabler-ui--docs-editor#repositionOverlay"
               role="tab" aria-selected="true" class="nav-link active">Preview</a>
          </li>
          <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
            <a href="#docs-editor-structure" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-tabler-ui--tab-target="toggle"
               role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="nav-link">Structure</a>
          </li>
          <li class="nav-item" role="presentation">
            <a href="#docs-editor-code" data-bs-toggle="tab" data-tabler-ui--tab-target="toggle"
               role="tab" aria-selected="false" class="nav-link">Code</a>
          </li>
        </ul>
        <div class="tab-content docs-editor-rail-body">
          <%# .docs-editor-preview-pane (docs.css) carries this pane down the
              height chain from .docs-editor-rail so the iframe's own
              height: 100% has something concrete to resolve against --
              without it, a .tab-pane has no height of its own, and the
              iframe falls back to its min-height instead of filling the
              pane (see that rule's own comment for the full chain). A
              modifier class on this one tab-pane, not .tab-pane itself,
              since the Structure and Code tab-panes are sized by their
              content and must not be forced to the rail's full height. %>
          <div class="tab-pane active show docs-editor-preview-pane" id="docs-editor-preview" role="tabpanel">
            <iframe src="<%= editor_frame_path %>" class="docs-editor-frame" title="Design preview"
                    data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="frame"></iframe>
          </div>
          <div class="tab-pane p-3" id="docs-editor-structure" role="tabpanel"
               data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="structure">
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">The current file's view tree renders here.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="tab-pane p-3" id="docs-editor-code" role="tabpanel"
               data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="code">
            <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">Generated .html.erb source renders here.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="col-12 col-lg-3 mb-3">
      <div class="card docs-editor-rail">
        <div class="card-header">
          <h3 class="card-title">Inspector</h3>
        </div>
        <div class="card-body docs-editor-rail-body" data-tabler-ui--docs-editor-target="inspector">
          <p class="text-secondary small mb-0">
            Select a node in the preview or the structure tree to edit its properties.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
